# Registry of every static-analysis suppression allowed in this repository.
# Checked by harness/guard/suppressions.sh.
# Format: <file> :: <directive> :: <trimmed source line>
# Prefer fixing the finding. Add an entry only with a reason in the comment above it.

# gosec G304: the file path is the constant policy location, not user input.
harness/guard/archcheck/main.go :: //nolint :: raw, err := os.ReadFile(file) //nolint:gosec // the policy path is a constant

# gosec G124: the Secure attribute is a setting, not a constant. A browser
# decides where a cookie may go by the scheme it sees, and over a link that
# is encrypted but not TLS - Tailscale, which is how this is looked at - a
# Secure cookie is stored by nobody. It defaults to true; turning it off is
# an operator saying they know the scheme is http and something else keeps
# the wire honest. See the function's own doc comment.
services/platform/internal/adapter/handler/session.go :: //nolint :: return &http.Cookie{ //nolint:gosec // Secure is a setting; see sessionCookie
services/platform/internal/adapter/handler/session.go :: //nolint :: return &http.Cookie{ //nolint:gosec // Secure is a setting; see this function's doc comment
